<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss economists maintain 1997, 1998 GDP forecasts.</title>
<headline>Swiss economists maintain 1997, 1998 GDP forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A quarterly survey of roughly 30 Swiss economists produced a nearly unchanged forecast for Swiss gross domestic product growth at 0.45 percent in 1997, and growth of 1.63 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>The results of the Swiss Business Economists' Consensus which produced the forecasts showed little change from the previous forecasts published March 25, when GDP was expected to grow 0.44 percent and 1.68 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>				1996	  1997	     1998</p>
<p> Real GDP growth (pct)  -0.7    +0.45 (0.44)   +1.63 (1.68)</p>
<p> Plant/equip investment -3.6    -0.98 (0.90)   +1.85 (2.62)</p>
<p> Real total exports     +2.5    +3.18 (3.33)   +4.29 (4.50)</p>
<p> Inflation		  +0.8    +0.84 (1.00)   +1.35 (1.60)</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	 4.7     5.46 (5.43)    5.26 (5.28)</p>
<p>Financial markets forecasts:</p>
<p>				24 Jun 97   End-Sept 97  End-June 98</p>
<p> Three-month Eurofrancs    1.36	    1.50	     2.15</p>
<p> Avg govt bond yield	 3.21	    3.38	     3.81</p>
<p> Mark/Swiss franc	   83.46	   83.81	    83.74</p>
<p> Dollar/Swiss franc	  1.439	   1.45	     1.43</p>
<p> Swiss Performance Index  3,525	   3,458	    3,559</p>
<p>Note: The latest survey was based on results from 32 economists in Swiss private banks and insurers, government agencies, universities, and labour unions. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
